#### 3. Lack of Fail-Fast Mechanisms

**Problem:** Current implementation continues attempting calls to obviously failing dependencies:

```csharp
// Current problematic implementation
public async Task<ClaimResult> ProcessClaim(Claim claim)
{
    try
    {
        // EDI service has been failing for 10 minutes, but we keep trying
        var ediResponse = await _ediClient.SubmitClaim(claim);
        return new ClaimResult { Success = true, Data = ediResponse };
    }
    catch (HttpRequestException ex)
    {
        // Log error and return failure - but we wasted 30 seconds timing out
        _logger.LogError(ex, "EDI submission failed for claim {ClaimId}", claim.Id);
        return new ClaimResult { Success = false, Error = "EDI service unavailable" };
    }
}
```

**Consequences:**
- Users wait 30+ seconds for timeout errors they'll receive anyway
- Resources wasted on calls that will obviously fail based on recent history
- No differentiation between "dependency temporarily slow" vs "dependency completely down"
- Operations team has no early warning signal of dependency health degradation

