#### Variation 3: Circuit Breaker with Exponential Backoff

**Use Case:** Dependencies with longer recovery times

**Implementation:**
```csharp
// Custom implementation with exponential backoff
public class ExponentialBackoffCircuitBreaker
{
    private int _openCount = 0;

    private TimeSpan GetOpenDuration()
    {
        // 30s, 60s, 120s, 240s, max 300s
        var seconds = Math.Min(30 * Math.Pow(2, _openCount), 300);
        return TimeSpan.FromSeconds(seconds);
    }

    private void OnCircuitOpened()
    {
        _openCount++;
        _durationOfBreak = GetOpenDuration();
    }

    private void OnCircuitClosed()
    {
        _openCount = 0;  // Reset on successful recovery
    }
}
```

**When to Use:**
- Dependencies known to have extended outages
- Reduce load on struggling services during recovery
- Scenarios where rapid retry attempts could worsen dependency issues

