### Real-World Example 1: EDI Gateway Integration with Circuit Breaker

**Context:**
The Claims Processing service submits 500K+ daily claims to an external EDI clearinghouse for electronic claim submission. The EDI gateway historically experiences periodic outages and latency spikes, particularly during high-volume periods (1st and 15th of each month when providers batch-submit claims). Before circuit breaker implementation, EDI issues caused complete claims service outages affecting all operations.

**Problem Scenario (Pre-Circuit Breaker):**
```text
June 2024 Incident Timeline:
09:15 AM - EDI clearinghouse begins experiencing latency (500ms → 45 seconds)
09:17 AM - Claims service connection pool exhausting (45/50 connections blocked)
09:19 AM - All 50 connections blocked waiting for EDI responses
09:20 AM - New claim submissions timing out (30-second timeout)
09:22 AM - Provider portal completely unavailable
09:25 AM - Kubernetes marks pods unhealthy, begins restart cycle
09:30 AM - Restart loop: Pods crash immediately on startup (same EDI issue)
09:45 AM - Emergency hotfix deployed: Hard-coded EDI bypass
10:15 AM - Full service restoration after EDI clearinghouse recovery
11:00 AM - Manual re-submission of 12,400 queued claims

Impact:

