### Real-World Example 2: Payment Gateway with Progressive Circuit Breaking

**Context:**
The Payment Service processes $150M+ monthly provider payments through an external payment gateway. The gateway has tiered failure modes: occasional timeouts (transient), partial outages (some payment types fail), and complete outages. Different failure modes require different circuit breaker strategies.

**Problem Scenario (Pre-Circuit Breaker):**
```text
Payment Processing Failure (March 2024):
01:00 AM - Nightly payment batch begins (8,500 providers, $47M total)
01:15 AM - Payment gateway intermittent timeouts (15% of requests)
01:30 AM - Service retrying all failures without intelligent backoff
01:45 AM - Thread pool exhausted (200 threads blocked on timeouts)
02:00 AM - OutOfMemoryError from accumulated timeout exceptions
02:15 AM - Payment service crashes, Kubernetes restart
02:20 AM - Restart loop: Same issue on startup (gateway still failing)
02:30 AM - Secondary payment service fails (shared cache overload)
03:00 AM - Manual intervention: Disable auto-retry, restart services
03:30 AM - Gateway recovers, but payment batch must start over
05:30 AM - Manual payment re-execution (requires auditor approval)
08:00 AM - Payment batch completes (7 hours total vs 2 hours normal)

Impact:

- 7-hour payment processing outage
- Provider payments delayed 24 hours
- $125K emergency processing fees
- $200K SLA penalty for late payments
- State financial reporting discrepancies
- Manual reconciliation required (3 days of effort)
```

**Implementation:**

**1. Multi-Level Circuit Breaker Strategy:**

```java
// PaymentGatewayCircuitBreakerConfig.java
@Configuration
public class PaymentGatewayCircuitBreakerConfig {

    // Level 1: Transient Failure Circuit Breaker (Lenient)
    @Bean
    public CircuitBreaker transientFailureCircuitBreaker() {
        CircuitBreakerConfig config = CircuitBreakerConfig.custom()
            .slidingWindowType(SlidingWindowType.TIME_BASED)
            .slidingWindowSize(60)                     // 60-second window
            .minimumNumberOfCalls(20)
            .failureRateThreshold(70)                  // Lenient: 70% threshold
            .slowCallRateThreshold(80)
            .slowCallDurationThreshold(Duration.ofSeconds(5))
            .waitDurationInOpenState(Duration.ofSeconds(15))  // Short break
            .permittedNumberOfCallsInHalfOpenState(5)
            .automaticTransitionFromOpenToHalfOpenEnabled(true)
            .recordExceptions(TimeoutException.class, ConnectException.class)
            .build();

        return CircuitBreakerRegistry.of(config).circuitBreaker("payment-transient");
    }

    // Level 2: Server Error Circuit Breaker (Strict)
    @Bean
    public CircuitBreaker serverErrorCircuitBreaker() {
        CircuitBreakerConfig config = CircuitBreakerConfig.custom()
            .slidingWindowType(SlidingWindowType.COUNT_BASED)
            .slidingWindowSize(10)
            .minimumNumberOfCalls(5)
            .failureRateThreshold(30)                  // Strict: 30% threshold
            .waitDurationInOpenState(Duration.ofSeconds(60))  // Longer break
            .permittedNumberOfCallsInHalfOpenState(2)
            .recordExceptions(
                HttpServerErrorException.class,
                ResourceAccessException.class
            )
            .build();

        return CircuitBreakerRegistry.of(config).circuitBreaker("payment-server-error");
    }

    // Level 3: Payment Type Circuit Breakers (Independent)
    @Bean
    public Map<PaymentType, CircuitBreaker> paymentTypeCircuitBreakers() {
        Map<PaymentType, CircuitBreaker> breakers = new HashMap<>();

        for (PaymentType type : PaymentType.values()) {
            CircuitBreakerConfig config = CircuitBreakerConfig.custom()
                .slidingWindowSize(20)
                .failureRateThreshold(50)
                .waitDurationInOpenState(Duration.ofSeconds(30))
                .build();

            breakers.put(type,
                CircuitBreakerRegistry.of(config)
                    .circuitBreaker("payment-" + type.name().toLowerCase()));
        }

        return breakers;
    }
}
```

**2. Service Implementation with Intelligent Fallback:**

```java
// PaymentService.java
@Service
public class PaymentService {

    private final CircuitBreaker transientCircuitBreaker;
    private final CircuitBreaker serverErrorCircuitBreaker;
    private final Map<PaymentType, CircuitBreaker> typeCircuitBreakers;
    private final PaymentGatewayClient gatewayClient;
    private final PaymentRetryQueue retryQueue;
    private final PaymentRepository repository;

    public CompletableFuture<PaymentResult> processPaymentAsync(Payment payment) {
        // Check payment-type-specific circuit breaker first
        CircuitBreaker typeBreaker = typeCircuitBreakers.get(payment.getType());
        if (typeBreaker.getState() == CircuitBreaker.State.OPEN) {
            logger.warn("Circuit open for payment type {}. Using fallback.",
                payment.getType());
            return CompletableFuture.completedFuture(
                executeTypeFallback(payment));
        }

        // Wrap in multi-level circuit breakers
        Supplier<CompletableFuture<PaymentResult>> supplier = () ->
            gatewayClient.submitPaymentAsync(payment);

        return Decorators.ofSupplier(supplier)
            .withCircuitBreaker(transientCircuitBreaker)
            .withCircuitBreaker(serverErrorCircuitBreaker)
            .withCircuitBreaker(typeBreaker)
            .withFallback(Arrays.asList(
                BrokenCircuitException.class,
                TimeoutException.class,
                HttpServerErrorException.class
            ), throwable -> {
                logger.warn("Circuit breaker fallback triggered for payment {}. Reason: {}",
                    payment.getId(), throwable.getMessage());
                return executeFallbackStrategy(payment, throwable);
            })
            .get()
            .get();  // Unwrap CompletableFuture<CompletableFuture<T>>
    }

    private PaymentResult executeFallbackStrategy(Payment payment, Throwable error) {
        // Fallback Strategy 1: Queue for later retry
        PaymentRetryMessage retryMessage = new PaymentRetryMessage();
        retryMessage.setPaymentId(payment.getId());
        retryMessage.setPaymentData(payment);
        retryMessage.setQueuedAt(LocalDateTime.now());
        retryMessage.setRetryCount(0);
        retryMessage.setMaxRetries(5);

        // Determine retry delay based on failure type
        Duration retryDelay;
        if (error instanceof BrokenCircuitException) {
            retryDelay = Duration.ofMinutes(5);  // Wait for circuit to close
        } else if (error instanceof TimeoutException) {
            retryDelay = Duration.ofMinutes(2);  // Quick retry for timeouts
        } else {
            retryDelay = Duration.ofMinutes(10); // Longer wait for server errors
        }

        retryMessage.setScheduledFor(LocalDateTime.now().plus(retryDelay));
        retryQueue.enqueue(retryMessage);

        // Update payment status
        payment.setStatus(PaymentStatus.PENDING_RETRY);
        payment.setLastErrorMessage(error.getMessage());
        payment.setNextRetryAt(LocalDateTime.now().plus(retryDelay));
        repository.save(payment);

        logger.info("Payment {} queued for retry in {} minutes",
            payment.getId(), retryDelay.toMinutes());

        return PaymentResult.builder()
            .status("PENDING_RETRY")
            .message("Payment gateway unavailable - queued for automatic retry")
            .paymentId(payment.getId())
            .willRetryAt(LocalDateTime.now().plus(retryDelay))
            .build();
    }

    private PaymentResult executeTypeFallback(Payment payment) {
        // Payment type circuit is open - try alternative payment method
        if (payment.getType() == PaymentType.ACH) {
            // ACH circuit open, try check payment as alternative
            logger.info("ACH circuit open for payment {}. Considering check payment.",
                payment.getId());

            // Queue for check payment processing
            checkPaymentQueue.enqueue(payment);

            return PaymentResult.builder()
                .status("CONVERTED_TO_CHECK")
                .message("ACH unavailable - converted to check payment")
                .paymentId(payment.getId())
                .alternativeMethod("CHECK")
                .processingDate(LocalDate.now().plusDays(3))
                .build();
        }

        // No alternative available, queue for retry
        return executeFallbackStrategy(payment,
            new BrokenCircuitException("Payment type circuit open"));
    }
}
```

